Janis Papanagnou wrote:

> you can't even revoke an article with google

Sure you can. If you're the author of a current
article shown on Google Groups, when you click
"show options", an additional link for you as the
article author, "remove", is displayed that does
not get displayed for those not the author of the
article.

This only works if your user-ID "now" matches
the user-ID under which you posted the article,
yet another reason to use a consistent posting
identity.

There is a separate problem, though, which is
that due to the many, many forged cancels over
the years, probably a majority of news server
sites don't honor article cancel messages at
all any more. Google Groups is one that still
does.

